{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanMarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Rat","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.family_a_h_minus_bridge_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.family_a_h_minus_bridge_pos","kind":"theorem","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L402-L425","doc":"**Strict positivity of the Family-A-vs-Jones gap for non-zero h.**\n\nFor every non-zero rational h, the Family-A-minus-bridge\ndifference is strictly positive, confirming that Family A is\nstructurally HIGHER than the Jones bridge at every q ≠ 1.\n\nThis formalises the empirical observation in PR #1272's witness\nthat Family A's residual versus the CODATA target (+0.0808 at\nq₀) exceeds the Jones bridge's residual (+0.0424) — the two\nroutes never coincide for h ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.family_a_h_minus_bridge_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.family_a_h_minus_bridge_explicit","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L363-L400","doc":"**The explicit Family-A-vs-Jones-bridge disagreement.**\n\nFor every h with `h² + 4 ≠ 0` (i.e. for all rational h, since\n`h² + 4 > 0`):\n\n  `linking_weight_family_a_h(h) − linking_weight_bridge(h)\n    = (3/4)·h² + (12·h⁴ + 4·h⁶) / (h² + 4)`\n\nNumerically at the substrate `h₀ ≈ 0.209` this gap is `≈ 0.0385`,\nwhich matches the empirical residual reported in PR #1272's\nγγ-decomposition probe witness.\n\n**Categorical interpretation.**  Family A (Wedderburn dim sum on\nH_4) and the Jones bridge (H_3 Markov trace of β_Bor, additively\nrescaled to match Family A at h=0) are different theorems about\ndifferent objects — both correct, both Lean-proved.  The\ndocstring of Python's `borromean_markov_trace_h2` previously\nclaimed they agree at h² order via the bridge; this is FALSE\nunder the Kauffman-Jones standard normalisation `[2]_q² =\nq² + 2 + q⁻²` (which IS the convention used here).  Under a\nnon-standard normalisation `(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})² = q + 2 + q⁻¹`\nthey appear to agree at h², but that is a normalisation\ncoincidence — see `docs/audits/2026-05-25-non-abelian-stokes-\nreading-a-exploration.md` and PR #1272's correction commit.\n\nThe open question is which of the two objects is the\ncategorically-correct `linking_weight` for the mass formula\n`m(𝓑₃) = m_e · Vol(𝓑₃)/ℏ_q² · linking_weight(q)`.  Neither\nmatches the CODATA-anchor target exactly; the Jones bridge is\n~47% closer than Family A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.linking_weight_family_a_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.linking_weight_family_a_h","kind":"def","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L357-L361","doc":"The Family-A linking-weight in h-form (mirror of\n`lambdaA_hForm` from `lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean`, restated\nhere over ℚ for consistency with `trM_borromean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.linking_weight_bridge_simplified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.linking_weight_bridge_simplified","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L337-L355","doc":"**Bridge simplification theorem.**  The bridge formula, written\nas a single rational function in h:\n\n`linking_weight_bridge(h) = 5/2 − (12·h⁴ + 4·h⁶) / (h² + 4)`\n\nDerivation: `4 · (trM − 1) = 4 · (num − den) / den\n= 4 · (−3h⁴ − h⁶) / (h² + 4) = −(12h⁴ + 4h⁶) / (h² + 4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.linking_weight_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.linking_weight_bridge","kind":"def","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L325-L335","doc":"The Jones-bridge form of `linking_weight(𝓑₃, q)`, written in h:\n\n`linking_weight_bridge(h) := 5/2 + 4·(trM_borromean(h) − 1)`\n\nThe `+5/2` and the factor `4` are CHOSEN to align with Family A's\nleading at h=0; they are not derived from the Markov trace itself.\n\nSee `family_a_h_minus_bridge_explicit` below for the explicit\nrational-function disagreement with Family A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Q_borromean_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Q_borromean_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L276-L293","doc":"**The bar-anti-symmetric companion of the Borromean Markov trace\nvanishes identically.** Direct consequence of\n`trM_borromean_bar_invariant`.\n\nCategorical interpretation: the Borromean braid 𝓑₃ carries no\nbar-anti-symmetric (Coulomb / EM-channel) component in its\nMarkov trace. This contrasts with the torus family `T(2, 2m)`,\nwhose `Q_m` is non-zero and equals `sinh((2m+1) η) / (2 cosh η)`\nat substrate (PR #1153).\n\nCloses the `Q_borromean_eq_zero : True := trivial` placeholder\nin `QOU.BraidKnot.BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities` (added\nby commit `d4d640ce7`, flagged as the next concrete Lean gap by\nPR #1196's audit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Q_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Q_borromean","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L267-L274","doc":"The bar-anti-symmetric companion of the Borromean Markov trace:\n`Q_borromean(h) := (tr_M(h) − tr_M(−h)) / 2`.\n\nDefined by analogy with `Q_m` from PR #1153 for the torus family\n`T(2, 2m)`, where `Q_m(h) = (q^{2m+1} − q^{−(2m+1)}) / (2 [2]_q)`\nis the odd-h projection of the full Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L259-L265","doc":"The Borromean Markov trace is invariant under the bar-involution\n`h ↦ −h` (equivalently `q ↦ q⁻¹`).  Archimedean shadow of\n`isBorromeanMarkovTrace_neg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h4_leading_coefficient_eq_neg_three_quarters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h4_leading_coefficient_eq_neg_three_quarters","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L252-L257","doc":"The leading h⁴ coefficient of (tr_M − 1) is exactly −3/4,\nobtained by evaluating the right factor at h = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_minus_one_factors_through_h_to_the_fourth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_minus_one_factors_through_h_to_the_fourth","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L230-L250","doc":"**Structural h² = 0 and h⁴ leading-order corollary.**\nThe Borromean Markov trace minus its h=0 value (which is 1)\nfactors through h⁴ — i.e. there is no h⁰, h¹, h², h³ correction:\n$$\\mathrm{tr}_M(\\beta_{\\mathrm{Bor}}, q) - 1\n   = h^4 \\cdot \\frac{-3 - h^2}{h^2 + 4}.$$\nThe leading h⁴ coefficient is therefore the value of the right\nfactor at h = 0, which is $-3/4$.\n\nThis makes the h² = 0 structural fact explicit (no Taylor-series\nmachinery needed; it follows by algebraic division of the\nrational expression).  Archimedean shadow of\n`borromean_markov_trace_closed_form_mul`.\n\nAudit chain: `docs/audits/2026-05-24-derivation-chain-gb-jet-orders-and-pentagon.md`\n(T1 closure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_markov_trace_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_markov_trace_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L217-L228","doc":"Main result: the Borromean Markov trace, combining all steps.\nV(𝓑₃) / [2]_q² = (4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶) / (h² + 4)\nwith the h² coefficient being exactly zero (cancellation).\n\nQuotient-form shadow of `borromean_markov_trace_closed_form_mul`; the\ndivision here is legitimate because `[2]_q² = h² + 4 ≠ 0`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:borromean-markov-trace-closed-form","label":"prop:borromean-markov-trace-closed-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/borromean-markov-trace-closed-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_at_h_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_at_h_zero","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L212-L215","doc":"At h = 0 (q = 1), the Markov trace is exactly 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_isTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_isTrace","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L203-L210","doc":"**The quotient form satisfies the multiplicative defining relation.**\nBridges the `ℚ` division form to the `R[h]` characterisation\n`IsBorromeanMarkovTrace`: `[2]_q² · (num/den) = num`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_den_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_den_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L199-L201","doc":"The denominator is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_den_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_den_pos","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L194-L197","doc":"The denominator is always positive (hence non-zero) for real h. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L189-L192","doc":"The Borromean Markov trace as a rational function of h (archimedean\nquotient form).  Pinned by `IsBorromeanMarkovTrace` once `[2]_q²` is\ninvertible — see `trM_borromean_isTrace`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.isBorromeanMarkovTrace_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.isBorromeanMarkovTrace_neg","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L172-L178","doc":"**Bar-invariance of the defining relation.**  A value `t` is the\nBorromean Markov trace at `h` iff it is the trace at `−h`.  Division-free\nconsequence of the evenness of numerator and denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_den_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_den_even","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L166-L170","doc":"The denominator polynomial `h² + 4` is even in `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_num_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_num_even","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L160-L164","doc":"The numerator polynomial `4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶` is even in `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_markov_trace_closed_form_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_markov_trace_closed_form_mul","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L134-L149","doc":"**Closed form, multiplicative (`R[h]`).**  Any `t` satisfying the\ndefining relation `IsBorromeanMarkovTrace h t` satisfies the exact\nmultiplicative identity\n\n  `[2]_q² · (t − 1) = −3h⁴ − h⁶ = h⁴·(−3 − h²)`.\n\nThis is the division-free statement of `tr_M = 1 + (−3h⁴ − h⁶)/[2]_q²`:\nafter clearing `[2]_q²`, the correction `[2]_q²·(tr_M − 1)` is a pure\nmultiple of `h⁴`, with no `h⁰…h³` term (the structural `h² = 0` fact).\n(No `Dvd` claim is made: over a generic ring this identity need not\nyield a quotient witness for `t − 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h2_coefficient_cancellation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h2_coefficient_cancellation","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L122-L132","doc":"**The `h² = 0` cancellation, multiplicatively.**\nThe numerator splits as `[2]_q²·1 + (−3h⁴ − h⁶)` — i.e. the `h⁰…h²`\npart of the numerator is *exactly* the denominator `4 + h²`, so a `t`\nsatisfying the defining relation has `t − 1` divisible by `[2]_q²` with\na pure-`h⁴` tail (`tr_M = 1 + (−3h⁴ − h⁶)/[2]_q²`, no `h¹,h²,h³`).\nPure `ring`, no division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h4_coefficient_of_num","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h4_coefficient_of_num","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L114-L120","doc":"The h⁴ coefficient of the numerator is −3.\nSince the denominator's leading term is 4,\nthe h⁴ coefficient of tr_M is −3/4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bracket2_to_trM_den","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bracket2_to_trM_den","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L108-L112","doc":"The substitution u = h² + 2 maps [2]² to the denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jones_to_trM_num","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jones_to_trM_num","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L101-L106","doc":"The substitution u = h² + 2 maps the Jones polynomial\nto the numerator of tr_M. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jones_division","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jones_division","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L93-L99","doc":"The polynomial division: V / [2]² = quotient + 16/(u+2).\nEquivalently: V = (u+2) · (−u² + 5u − 9) + 16. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bracket2_sq_in_u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bracket2_sq_in_u","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L90-L91","doc":"[2]_q² = (q + q⁻¹)² in terms of u = q² + q⁻². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jones_borromean_in_u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jones_borromean_in_u","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L87-L88","doc":"The Jones polynomial of the Borromean rings in u = q² + q⁻². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.isBorromeanMarkovTrace_one_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.isBorromeanMarkovTrace_one_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L81-L85","doc":"At `h = 0` (q = 1), `t = 1` solves the defining relation: `4·1 = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsBorromeanMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsBorromeanMarkovTrace","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L69-L79","doc":"**The defining multiplicative relation for the Borromean Markov trace.**\nA value `t : R` *is* the Borromean Markov trace at `h` iff\n\n  `[2]_q² · t = numerator`,   i.e.   `(h² + 4)·t = 4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶`.\n\nThis replaces the division-form `tr_M := num/den`, characterising `tr_M`\nWITHOUT inverting `[2]_q²`, so it makes sense over any `R[h]`.  Over a\nfield where `h² + 4 ≠ 0` it pins `t = num/den` uniquely (see\n`trM_borromean_isTrace` in the `ℚ` section). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_den","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_den","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L66-L67","doc":"The denominator `[2]_q² = h² + 4` as a polynomial in h. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_num","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_num","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The numerator of tr_M(β_Bor) as a polynomial in h: `4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}